-- two atoms in the same orbit, witnessed: an automorphism carrying one to the other. The witness is
-- kept rather than truncated, so the witness itself is available to any observation; truncating it
-- (‖·‖, §8.3) makes the relation a proposition and is written when the library's Trunc is settled.
Orbit : (M : Mol) → mol-atoms M → mol-atoms M → Type 0
Orbit M x y = (a : Auto M) × (auto-fun M a x ≡ y)
